/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - A person becomes part of a circuit when two points of the body touch a live conductor and a return path.
   - Skin is the main resistor.
   - I is the body current in amperes, V is the touch voltage in volts, and R is the resistance of the current path in ohms.
   - Path matters because current density matters.
   - At 50 Hz or 60 Hz the effects rise in a fixed order as current increases.
   - Why is 50/60 Hz the worst frequency?
   - Duration changes the outcome.
   - Macro-shock means current enters through intact skin.
   - Micro-shock means an insulated conductor, a saline-filled catheter or a pacing lead carries current directly to the heart.
   - Micro-shock also depends on timing.
*/
